  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Every public method that takes a CancellationToken takes it last and optional (= default), so a caller that does not cancel leaves it out. Migration chains without a hand-kept list: a database without entities declares its chain as an [LdbMigrations] partial class, each version derives from VersionedMigration<TChain>, and the package's generator (shipped inside it) writes TChain.Migrations with every version in order; LDB2015 and LDB2016 for a chain or version it cannot use. MigrateAsync takes over tables a database got before its first migration (EnsureTablesAsync), applying the unfixed model to them as they are.",
